    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0117" n="61" xml:id="pg61"/>

                <head>No. 44.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-07-01"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 1, 1876</date>.
                        (Received August 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 97.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Senatorial Chinese Investigating
                    Committee of California have addressed to Dr. Williams a series of sixteen
                    questions bearing upon the subject of their investigation, which he has
                    answered. He has prepared and handed to me the inclosed copy of the queries and
                    his responses. This I send to you for the files of the Department. He has told
                    me that he will send the original paper to you with the request that you will
                    forward it to the committee if you see no good reason to the contrary.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE F. SEWARD.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d44-a1.xml" xpointer="d44-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
